https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oxHnRfhDmrk  (Capo 0) (MC0)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  There are a couple of chords only played once.  The (Cm) is played like a (Bm) on the 3rd fret and is only played once, in the bridge on the word "starry".  In the last verse, there's one lonely (Asus2) sandwiched in between two (Am)'s or the word "still".  Just lift off the index finger from the (Am).  And the last chord in the song is a (Gadd) in which you just add your ring finger to the 2nd string above the 1st finger.   

TIP:  At the end there's a nifty little walk-up all played in the 2nd fret (notes may or may not transpose).  You'll end on the (Gadd) so hold the (G) form and use the pad of your index finger to press down on the strings in an on/off pattern.  Untransposed, the notes are:  open 4th string <d>, 4th string/2nd fret <e>, open 3rd string <g>, 3rd string/2nd fret <a>, open 2nd string <b>.  (These are the same notes as "starry starry night.")  Then pause for a moment and pick the final note, 1st string/3rd fret <g>.  Easy. 
   
       
